xnu 0197: apollo_idle=1 (display-dark power saving) and an honest memory-bus vote log

Why the SWEET CPUFREQ lines said "memory bus at its top 100% of the time" with every core quiet (boot-quiet1, boot-perm2): not a
failed vote. 0158 made sweetddr=2 (always at the top) the default; sweet_rpmh_ddr_set() then returns ENOTSUP before voting (the
sweet_rpmh_ddr_set(false) call is reached but refused), and the governor (0153) keeps counting the bus as at its top, while still
printing "the memory bus following the load". Boot 88 (sweetddr=1) had reset with the display on after the vote dropped (not proven).

This patch: SWEET RPMH: memory bus lowered/raised (reason) on each change, "... FAILED: errno N" on a failed vote (3 failures:
not tried again for a while), "memory bus stays at its top" once when pinned; the CPUFREQ line says "(pinned by sweetddr=2)".

New option apollo_idle=1 (boot-arg or mkadt.py --option; DEFAULT 0 = behaviour unchanged). Once the display has been off and dark for
3 s (sweet_display_dark): governor 100 ms/sample (apollo_idle_gov_ms), keys 80 ms, vsync timer 200 ms, GPU watchdog 2 s, sweetlog
flush 30 s, Wi-Fi MHI 10 ms, net thread 5/25 ms, backboardd profiler paused, memory bus lowered to sweetddrlow when quiet
(apollo_idle_ddr=0: left alone). Restored at once when the display turns on. "SWEET IDLE:" line on each change.
